{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, and YHWH drove the sea with a strong east wind, etc.</b> It was His will, blessed be He, to split the sea with a drying east wind, so that it would appear as though the wind itself was the one drying up the sea, as in the matter that is written (Hosea 13:15), \"An east wind, the wind of YHWH, shall come, and his spring shall be dried up, and his fountain shall fail.\" He dealt superbly with Egypt and destroyed them, for because of this they perhaps thought that the wind had set the sea dry, and that it was not the hand of YHWH that had done this for Israel's sake — even though the wind does not split a sea into pieces, they did not set their mind to this either. And they came after them because of the abundance of their desire to do them harm. And this is the meaning of \"I will harden Pharaoh's heart and he will come after them\" — for He hardened their heart to say, \"I will pursue my enemies and overtake them in the sea, and there is none who saves from my hand.\" And they did not remember now that YHWH had fought for them against Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:13.893783170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}